WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.700
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.601
Unit six: Community Life. Today you will talk about ability and suggestions with can and could.

4
00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.391
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:21.926
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:23.866
Civic duty.

7
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.324
Civic duty means what a good citizen should do for society.

8
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:30.591
Voting is a civic duty.

9
00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:33.963
Your turn. Say: Civic duty.

10
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.964
Civic duty.

11
00:00:38.717 --> 00:00:39.776
Volunteer.

12
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:43.758
Volunteer means to work without pay to help others.

13
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.930
I volunteer at the library on Saturdays.

14
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:50.482
Your turn. Say: Volunteer.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.451
Volunteer.

16
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:56.195
Neighborly.

17
00:00:57.183 --> 00:01:00.321
Neighborly means friendly and helpful to people nearby.

18
00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:02.730
Our street is very neighborly.

19
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:06.015
Your turn. Say: Neighborly.

20
00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:09.821
Neighborly.

21
00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:11.979
Local initiative.

22
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:16.631
Local initiative means a project started by people in the area.

23
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:19.518
A local initiative cleaned the canal.

24
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:22.815
Your turn. Say: Local initiative.

25
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.260
Local initiative.

26
00:01:28.017 --> 00:01:28.890
Charity.

27
00:01:29.883 --> 00:01:32.963
Charity means an organization that helps people in need.

28
00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.248
We raised money for a charity.

29
00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.328
Your turn. Say: Charity.

30
00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.005
Charity.

31
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:43.612
Donate.

32
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:47.092
Donate means to give money or things to help.

33
00:01:47.683 --> 00:01:49.834
We donated clothes after the flood.

34
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.940
Your turn. Say: Donate.

35
00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:56.743
Donate.

36
00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.461
Collaborate.

37
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.937
Collaborate means to work together with others.

38
00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.782
Students collaborate on the project.

39
00:02:05.383 --> 00:02:07.827
Your turn. Say: Collaborate.

40
00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:11.633
Collaborate.

41
00:02:12.383 --> 00:02:13.512
Grassroots.

42
00:02:14.517 --> 00:02:17.793
Grassroots means started by ordinary people, not leaders.

43
00:02:18.383 --> 00:02:20.162
It was a grassroots movement.

44
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.727
Your turn. Say: Grassroots.

45
00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:27.591
Grassroots.

46
00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.328
Outreach.

47
00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:33.350
Outreach means work to help people outside your group.

48
00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.228
The clinic does outreach in villages.

49
00:02:36.817 --> 00:02:39.144
Your turn. Say: Outreach.

50
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.036
Outreach.

51
00:02:43.783 --> 00:02:44.947
Support system.

52
00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.948
Support system means people who help you when you need it.

53
00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.468
My neighbours are my support system.

54
00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:54.666
Your turn. Say: Support system.

55
00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.733
Support system.

56
00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:00.821
Solidarity.

57
00:03:01.817 --> 00:03:05.209
Solidarity means standing together and supporting each other.

58
00:03:05.817 --> 00:03:08.478
The village showed solidarity after the storm.

59
00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:11.585
Your turn. Say: Solidarity.

60
00:03:14.433 --> 00:03:15.748
Solidarity.

61
00:03:16.483 --> 00:03:17.554
Contribute.

62
00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.583
Contribute means to give or help to make something succeed.

63
00:03:22.183 --> 00:03:24.125
Everyone can contribute something.

64
00:03:24.717 --> 00:03:27.520
Your turn. Say: Contribute.

65
00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:31.205
Contribute.

66
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.976
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:36.817 --> 00:03:40.117
Visal, how can students help the community?

68
00:03:41.217 --> 00:03:44.807
Students can volunteer at local events.

69
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:47.463
Any other ideas?

70
00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:51.861
We could organize a charity event for poor families.

71
00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:53.998
Who would help?

72
00:03:55.083 --> 00:04:00.174
We could collaborate with the local initiative. Everyone can contribute something.

73
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:02.752
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:03.617 --> 00:04:06.777
Grammar focus: can and could for ability & suggestion.

75
00:04:07.077 --> 00:04:08.310
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:09.017 --> 00:04:10.587
Students can volunteer.

77
00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:13.553
We could organize a charity event.

78
00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.403
Everyone can contribute something.

79
00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:22.248
Use 'can' for things people are able to do. Use 'could' to suggest an idea politely.

80
00:04:22.983 --> 00:04:26.564
Be careful! Don't say: Students can to volunteer.

81
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.906
Say: Students can volunteer.

82
00:04:31.206 --> 00:04:32.950
Don't use 'to' after 'can' or 'could'.

83
00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:36.373
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:38.853
Neighbours Helping Neighbours.

85
00:04:39.153 --> 00:04:42.627
Volunteering for a local initiative taught me about civic duty.

86
00:04:43.633 --> 00:04:47.281
Our neighbourhood is very neighborly and shows real solidarity.

87
00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:52.205
After the flood, people donated food and clothes to a charity.

88
00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.674
Students can collaborate with grassroots outreach groups.

89
00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.502
We could all contribute to a stronger support system.

90
00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:05.207
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:09.318
We blank organize a charity event. It's an idea.

92
00:05:09.618 --> 00:05:13.143
A, could. B, mustn't. C, couldn't.

93
00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.572
The answer is A: could.

94
00:05:19.717 --> 00:05:22.482
Standing together and supporting each other is blank.

95
00:05:22.782 --> 00:05:26.773
A, solidarity. B, outreach. C, charity.

96
00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:32.426
The answer is A: solidarity.

97
00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:35.885
To work together with others is to blank.

98
00:05:36.185 --> 00:05:40.128
A, collaborate. B, donate. C, contribute.

99
00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:45.689
The answer is A: collaborate.

100
00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.423
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:53.921
How can students contribute to their community?

102
00:06:02.717 --> 00:06:04.229
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:04.529 --> 00:06:13.555
Students can clean public places and teach younger children. We could also collect books and donate them to village schools.

104
00:06:13.855 --> 00:06:15.576
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:16.483 --> 00:06:21.783
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and can and could for ability & suggestion.

106
00:06:22.083 --> 00:06:26.302
Today's value is community spirit. Help and care for people in your town.

107
00:06:26.602 --> 00:06:28.895
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

108
00:06:29.195 --> 00:06:32.706
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

